module gunbc.design_ruling

import std.types { String }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import std.markdown { MarkdownDocument, MarkdownBlock, HeadingBlock, TextInline, H1 }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, p, hr }
import extdeps.languages.markdown { serialize_markdown_source }

// THE DATED OPERATOR RULINGS DESIGN.md STATES, HELD AS ROWS RATHER THAN NARRATED INLINE.
//
// gunbc.design_document carries reasoning; a ruling is a HISTORY fact -- when, in which section, and
// on whose words -- and it grows by one row per decision while the sections are fixed by section 1.
// The RULE has exactly one home, the document: a row carries no copy of it, so the two cannot drift.
// A row's `reference` is its own declaration as a DeclarationRef; the document cites a ruling by
// passing the row (an import, so a renamed or deleted row fails to resolve), and
// gunbc.documentary_refs takes its ruling references from design_rulings(), so that one roster is
// the population the citation resolver, the render witness and the view below all read.
//
// One row per ruling, each its own declaration, so a citation names one ruling and two lanes adding
// two rulings touch two declarations. The on-demand view is
// `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/design_ruling.dag --function expected_design_rulings_md`;
// it is not committed, for the same contention reason as the failure-mode ledger.

type DesignRuling {
  reference: DeclarationRef
  decided: String
  section: String
  provenance: String
}

data bmc_secure_goes_live_per_controller_family: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "bmc_secure_goes_live_per_controller_family"),
  decided: "2026-10-28",
  section: "3",
  provenance: "Operator answers to session cool-owl-599 on staffing the brief that retires gunbc.tools.bmc_onboard for BMC credential rotation. (1) The state-shaped BmcSecure (gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure cut O1b) may become the live authority for the ASRock ALTRAD8UD / OpenBMC family while the rotation-event path stays frozen as mtcollins1's standing under ruling C (eager-gull-22, 2026-10-04), on the condition that mtcollins1's own cutover is left near a flag switch rather than stranded: \"yeah thats fine assuming the code is basically a flag switch to finish the mtcollins migration - i don't want to leave it on an island/stranded\". (2) A build that forces the published credential's change on first login is behaviour modeled per version and interacted with, and in that state the password write is the first rotation; the converge rotates at the earliest point and never redundantly: \"thats behavior we have to model per version and interact with ... Our workflow should be smart enough to rotate credentials at the earliest place, and not do it redundantly\" (gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_credential_policy). (3) Failed-login probes against an account with a lockout budget are avoided where a derivation is available, and otherwise accounted for: \"we can't do lockout bound reads basically - or, we have to account for them - i would avoid it if possible\" (bmc_secure PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount). (4) srv1-srv4, the same board family, are in scope for the cutover; the Supermicro H11SSL units are folded in, with their per-unit bootstrap credential held in the operator's sheet for now.",
}

