data root_generalization_closes_breadth: DesignRuling = DesignRuling {
  reference: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "root_generalization_closes_breadth"),
  decided: "2026-10-16",
  section: "6b",
  provenance: "Operator ruling, amended 2026-10-16 after side-chat review: the method is named root generalization, with anti-unification (Plotkin) as its formal core, and lives in 6b beside chain re-derivation rather than in its own section. Root-cause repair fixes depth; this closes breadth. A new case that needs new code is first asked whether it is another instance of what existing leaves already do; if so, every leaf of that shape is collected, generalized to the least general rule at the earliest unjustified boundary (6b), and deleted (3, delete-first), repeating while the generalizations form a family. The horizontal half was filed as a_rule_is_applied_at_the_site_that_prompted_it_and_not_its_sibling with a recognition rule addressed to authors, which did not work: three fork families grew in one week while it existed (type-alias identity at node_type_compatible call sites, #13941 #14069 #13974 #14043 #14057; v1 Rust trait-bound pipelines, #13978 #14010 #14020; qualified-call resolution, #13925 #14085 #14089); positive specimens #14151 #14193 #13872 #14187). So the check is placed on the reviewer: a repeated pattern is rejected until the author answers with a stated reason not to generalize or a named trigger and follow-up, and the reviewer accepts or rejects that answer; no answer is a reject.",
}

